 "about": "Beech forest from about 900 m to the treeline at 2100 m, with silver fir, Italian maple, sycamore and holly; Calabrian pine forests on the Sila, the Aspromonte and Etna; Bosnian pines on the limestone ridges of the Pollino; Turkey, Hungarian, downy and sessile oak, sweet chestnut, Italian alder, hop hornbeam and manna ash below the beech, holm oak on rocky slopes and cork oak low in Sicily; tree heath, Spanish and common broom, hawthorn, hazel and prickly juniper in the clearings, common juniper on the pastures and dwarf juniper above the trees; bracken in the open woods, ferns, asphodel on the grazed ground, mat-grass on the Sila pastures, rush-leaved moor-grass on the limestone summits and alpine flowers; flocks of sheep and goats, grey Podolica cattle, free-ranging horses and black pigs; stone villages with low tile roofs.",
